      "writtenOn": "2026-04-23T23:53:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The order-only deps are passed into WriteStampOrPhonyForTarget, so the dependency still exists. The only difference this causes is that the phony rule now has an order-only dependency on the dependencies, instead of an implicit dependency. But I think this doesn\u0027t matter, because all dependencies on the bundle_data phony rule are order-only.\n\n- create_bundle targets depending on bundle_data will have an order-only dependency on the bundle_data phony rule. So transitive dependencies via the bundle_data edge will be treated as order-only.\n- Non-action, non-create_bundle targets will not have a dependency on the phony rule because of the check for BUNDLE_DATA in WriteInputDepsStampOrPhonyAndGetDep.\n- Action targets will have a dependency on the phony rule, created by the check for IsDataOnly() in NinjaActionTargetWriter::Run. However, this dependency is order-only, so the same reasoning applies as for create_bundle targets.\n\n(I also had Gemini double check my reasoning, and it agrees with me.)",
      "parentUuid": "0e3fd9dc_b0dbf7c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 0
